 "registered_text_amendments": [
  {
   "amendment": "the clause is completed in the missing direction, using the same pre-committed bar rather than a new threshold: it fires when NEITHER arm clears POOL_CONTROL_WIN_LIMIT against its own churn arm, since the two are then indistinguishable and no edge was shown to recommend Gate 4 on (label PASS_COST_ONLY_NO_DEMONSTRATED_EDGE, exit 2).",
   "boundary_reading": "Because 'has an edge' is binary at POOL_CONTROL_WIN_LIMIT, the clause also withholds when the adaptive arm is clearly better than the loss-blind arm (9 of 12 against 3 of 12) but neither clears the bar - variant adaptive_just_short_of_bar_loss_blind_far_below. Consequence of the amendment: authorizing Gate 4 now requires the adaptive arm to clear the bar AND the loss-blind arm not to, so the primary run's quality has to be demonstrated at the pre-committed bar rather than merely not-failed (the harm guard only rejects adaptive losing 10 of 12). This is the reading to contest if a sub-bar but real edge should authorize; recorded here rather than resolved silently.",
   "demonstrated_after": [
    {
     "label": "PASS_COST_ONLY_POOL_MATCHED_CONTROL_PASSES",
     "reads": "both arms clear the bar: a pool/location effect alone would have passed the gate",
     "variant": "pool_control_passes"
    },
    {
     "label": "PASS_COST_ONLY_NO_DEMONSTRATED_EDGE",
     "reads": "neither arm clears the bar: indistinguishable, no quality premise",
     "variant": "control_ties_adaptive_nobody_demonstrates_an_edge"
    }
   ],
   "demonstrated_before": {
    "consequence": "the state the registered wording says must withhold was the state the shipped rule authorized, and it is the state the dev-fidelity evidence predicts for the real path. The harm guard cannot catch it (it only rejects adaptive losing >= 10 of 12) and neither can the section 5.14 clause (churn against do-nothing, not adaptive against the loss-blind arm).",
    "observed_then": "adaptive 6/12, control 6/12 -> PASS, exit 0, Gate 4 AUTHORIZED",
    "variant": "control_ties_adaptive_nobody_demonstrates_an_edge"
   },
   "direction": "strictly tightening: it can only convert an authorization into a withholding, never the reverse, so no spent block is reinterpreted. Verified on the two committed real-path verdicts after the change (see section 5.44).",
   "registered_text": "if the pool-matched arm's quality is indistinguishable from the adaptive arm's, record the cost PASS but withhold the Gate 4 recommendation, since the quality premise would then be unsupported",
   "section": "5.5 change 3",
   "shipped_rule_before": "only one direction of the clause was implemented: it fired when the loss-blind arm beat its own churn arm on >= 10 of 12 pairs (POOL_CONTROL_WIN_LIMIT). No adaptive-vs-control comparison existed anywhere in v0_verdict.py.",
   "still_not_a_test": "'indistinguishable' is operationalised as both arms sitting on the same side of the bar, not as a statistical test of equality; recorded as a proxy."
  }
 ],
